=   refer parasite.Threading
-   refer parasite.Supervisor
+   refer parasite.Supervisor

-   entry .platformThreads   each task on a new platform thread: `PlatformSupervisor`
-   entry .virtualThreads   each task on a virtual thread: `VirtualSupervisor`
-       Needs Java 21 and fails at runtime on an older JVM; forks platform threads on Scala
-       Native, where there is no Loom.
-   entry .adaptiveThreads   virtual threads where the JVM has them, platform threads otherwise: `AdaptiveSupervisor`
-   entry .pooledThreads   tasks on reusable carrier threads: `PooledSupervisor`
-       For fine-grained fan-out, where a thread start per task would dominate; a task has no
-       thread of its own, so thread-locals persist across the tasks a carrier runs.
-   entry .javascriptThreads   tasks run eagerly at their fork, on one strand: `JavascriptSupervisor`
-       The model for Scala.js, with the limits of a single strand: no interleaving, instant
-       sleeps, and a panic on a wait which no completed task could ever end.
+   entry .platformThreads   cada tarefa numa nova thread de plataforma: `PlatformSupervisor`
+   entry .virtualThreads   cada tarefa numa thread virtual: `VirtualSupervisor`
+       Precisa de Java 21 e falha em tempo de execução numa JVM mais antiga; cria threads de
+       plataforma com fork no Scala Native, onde não há Loom.
+   entry .adaptiveThreads   threads virtuais onde a JVM as tem, threads de plataforma caso contrário: `AdaptiveSupervisor`
+   entry .pooledThreads   tarefas em threads portadoras reutilizáveis: `PooledSupervisor`
+       Para fan-out de granularidade fina, em que iniciar uma thread por tarefa dominaria o
+       custo; uma tarefa não tem thread própria, de modo que os thread-locals persistem entre as
+       tarefas que uma portadora executa.
+   entry .javascriptThreads   tarefas executadas de forma ansiosa no seu fork, num único fio: `JavascriptSupervisor`
+       O modelo para o Scala.js, com os limites de um único fio: nenhum entrelaçamento, sleeps
+       instantâneos, e um pânico numa espera que nenhuma tarefa concluída poderia jamais
+       encerrar.

